# Machine-local settings for talknest. Copy to local.env (git-ignored) and
# edit: every start_*.sh script loads it, so no per-invocation arguments
# are needed. Every entry is optional and only overrides a script default.
#
#   cp local.env.example local.env
#
# Nothing here belongs in version control: it describes where this machine
# keeps its venvs, builds and weights.

# ---- paths ----

# Root holding the model weights (GGUF, Qwen3-ASR, Qwen3-TTS, Silero VAD).
# Default: the "model" directory next to this checkout.
# TALKNEST_MODEL_ROOT=/path/to/model

# venv that provides vllm or qwen-asr-serve for ASR.
# ASR_VENV=/path/to/venv

# llama.cpp build directory (must contain llama-server) for the 9B LLM.
# TN9B_BIN_DIR=/path/to/llama.cpp/build/bin

# 27B profile only: external launcher and the model's chat template.
# RUN_QWEN38=/path/to/run_qwen38.sh
# QWEN38_CHAT_TEMPLATE=/path/to/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4/chat_template.jinja

# ---- GPU sizing (card dependent) ----

# Share of *total* VRAM for the ASR pool. 0.06 suits a large unified pool,
# 0.50 a 12G card; below 0.45 vLLM refuses to start.
# ASR_GPU_UTIL=0.06
# ASR_MAX_BATCHED=2048
# ASR_MAX_SEQS=2

# Weight quantization for ASR, e.g. fp8. Halves the weights, so pair it
# with a smaller ASR_GPU_UTIL to actually free VRAM for the LLM. Unset
# keeps the checkpoint dtype.
# ASR_QUANT=fp8

# Pin llama.cpp GPU layers instead of letting -fit choose them.
# TN9B_NGL=36

# ---- orchestrator ----

# A LAN browser only exposes the microphone over HTTPS, so point these at
# the cert from scripts/gen_dev_cert.sh.
# TLS_CERT=certs/dev.pem
# TLS_KEY=certs/dev.key
# TALKNEST_PORT=8890
